ptions tailored to your preferences.</p></details><details class=\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 group\"><summary class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\">How do I choose the best name for my Achilles Tang?</summary><p class=\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">Choosing the perfect name for your Achilles Tang 🐠 depends on their personality, appearance, and your personal taste! Observe your Achilles Tang&#x27;s unique behaviors — are they playful or calm? Bold or shy? Pick a name that feels right when you say it aloud. Short, 1-2 syllable names often work best as they are easier for animals to recognize and respond to.</p></details><details class=\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 group\"><summary class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\">Can I use human names for my Achilles Tang?</summary><p class=\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">Absolutely! Human names are very popular for Achilles Tangs 🐠. Names like Oliver, Sophie, Jack, or Emma work wonderfully and add a personal, meaningful touch. Many pet owners prefer human names because they create a stronger emotional connection and feel more like a family member than just a pet.</p></details><details class=\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 group\"><summary class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\">What are some unique Achilles Tang names?</summary><p class=\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">For unique Achilles Tang names 🐠, consider fantasy-inspired options, names from foreign languages, or creative invented combinations. Our Fantasy Names and Unique Names categories feature one-of-a-kind options drawn from mythology, literature, and pure imagination. You can also draw inspiration from your favorite books, movies, or video games!</p></details><details class=\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 group\"><summary class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\">Should my Achilles Tang&#x27;s name be easy to pronounce?</summary><p class=\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">Yes! Choose a name that is easy for you and your family to say consistently 🐠. Avoid names that sound too similar to common commands (like &quot;Kit&quot; for &quot;Sit&quot;). A clear, distinct name helps your Achilles Tang recognize when you are calling them and strengthens training effectiveness.</p></details><details class=\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 group\"><summary class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\">What makes a good name for a Achilles Tang?</summary><p class=\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">A good Achilles Tang name is clear, easy to pronounce, and fits your pet&#x27;s personality. Avoid names that sound like commands or household names. The best names often come from observing your Achilles Tang&#x27;s habits and character — the right name will feel natural after a few days of use.</p></details><details class=\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 group\"><summary class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\">Can I give my Achilles Tang a humorous or unusual name?</summary><p class=\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">Absolutely — humorous and unusual names often become beloved conversation starters. The key is ensuring the name brings you joy rather than embarrassment when called in public. If you smile every time you say it, it&#x27;s the right name regardless of convention.</p></details></div></section><section class=\"max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-center mb-8\">📖 <!-- -->Achilles Tang<!-- --> Naming Guide</h2><div class=\"bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm border border-gray-100\"><ul class=\"space-y-3\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-primary font-bold text-lg\">0<!-- -->1</span><span>Consider your achilles tang&#x27;s personality — is it bold, shy, playful, or calm?</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-primary font-bold text-lg\">0<!-- -->2</span><span>Look at physical traits like color, size, or unique markings.</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-primary font-bold text-lg\">0<!-- -->3</span><span>Say the name out loud — does it sound natural and easy to call?</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-primary font-bold text-lg\">0<!-- -->4</span><span>Avoid names that sound like common commands or other pets&#x27; names.</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-primary font-bold text-lg\">0<!-- -->5</span><span>Try out a few names and see which one your achilles tang responds to best.</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-primary font-bold text-lg\">0<!-- -->6</span><span>Short names (1-2 syllables) tend to be easiest for animals to learn and recognize.</span></li></ul></div></section><section class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-10 space-y-10\"><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8\"><div><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-center mb-6\">🔗 <!-- -->Achilles Tang<!-- --> Name Categories</h2><div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\"><a class=\"bg-white rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 hover:border-primary hover:text-primary transition-all\" href=\"/achilles-tang-names/\">📛<!-- --> <!-- -->Achilles Tang<!-- --> <!-- -->Names</a><a class=\"bg-white rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 hover:border-primary hover:text-primary transition-all\" href=\"/male-achilles-tang-names/\">♂️<!-- --> <!-- -->Achilles Tang<!-- --> <!-- -->Male Names</a><a class=\"bg-white rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 hover:border-primary hover:text-primary transition-all\" href=\"/f